# =============================================================================
# WiiU-GP-RE — DEFAULT-DENY .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# Strategy: ignore EVERYTHING at the workspace root, then explicitly re-include
# the small set of paths that are original work. A new directory, a newly
# downloaded tarball, or a fresh `git clone` of someone else's project can never
# be committed by accident — it stays ignored until someone deliberately adds an
# allowlist rule below and reviews it.
#
# This is the inverse of the usual .gitignore (which is deny-list based and
# therefore fails open). For a repo whose entire purpose is publishing original
# reverse-engineering work that was developed *next to* cloned GPL/BSD trees,
# failing closed is the only safe default.
#
# To publish a new path, add a `!` rule in the ALLOWLIST section and re-run:
#     bash WiiU-tk/_meta/prepublish-audit.sh
# =============================================================================

# --- 1. DENY EVERYTHING ------------------------------------------------------
/*
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!README.md
!LICENSE
!THIRD-PARTY.md

# --- 2. ALLOWLIST: original work only ---------------------------------------
# The toolkit is self-contained: scripts, our own C/C++ test harnesses, docs,
# and our own diffs against upstream. Nothing here is a copy of a third-party
# source tree.
!/WiiU-tk/

# =============================================================================
# 3. BELT AND BRACES
# =============================================================================
# The rules below are redundant while rule 1 is in force. They are kept as
# documentation of *why* each path is excluded, and they keep protecting the
# repo if somebody ever deletes the deny-all rule.

# --- vendored third-party source trees (NEVER publish) ----------------------
# pc2drc               thefloppydriver/pc2drc — GPLv2, full clone w/ our edits
# build/hostap-2.12    hostapd — GPLv2, patched in place
# research/*           libdrc (BSD-2), wozt-libdrc (BSD-2), barista (GPLv2),
#                      drc-hostap (GPLv2) — all full clones with .git history
# kernel/              Kali linux-source-7.1 (GPLv2) + .deb + build artefacts
/pc2drc/
/build/
/kernel/
/research/
/out/
/capture/
/run/
/tests/

# --- console secrets and personal data (NEVER publish) ---------------------
# pairing.env holds a live 64-hex WPA2 PSK, the console BSSID and pad MAC
# recovered from a real WPS pairing. Leaking it lets anyone impersonate the AP.
pairing.env
*.env
.env
get_psk.conf
psk.conf
*_psk*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12

# --- local-only deny patterns for the pre-publish audit --------------------
# This file holds the *actual* console MAC/BSSID/PSK so the audit script itself
# can stay publishable without containing them. Must never be committed.
.private-deny-patterns
*.private-patterns

# --- captures and binary evidence -----------------------------------------
# The captured WPS credential-delivery frame holds the console SSID and the
# plaintext 64-hex PSK as ASCII inside the binary record. It is a legitimately
# interesting protocol artifact, but it is a live credential, so it stays out.
WiiU-tk/09-rce-hunt/tables/uic-792-reply0.bin

# 1.3 GB of pcaps containing a real encrypted console<->pad session, plus the
# extracted UDP payload dumps. Not third-party *code*, but it is someone's live
# device traffic and it bloats the repo past GitHub's limits anyway.
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.pcap.gz
*.cap
*.ivs
*.h264
*.264
*.ts
*.mp4
*.mkv

# --- memory images: these contain keys, MACs and pairing state -------------
core
core.*
vgcore.*
*.core
*.dmp
*.mem

# --- build products and compiled objects -----------------------------------
*.o
*.ko
*.so
*.so.*
*.a
*.lo
*.la
*.lib
*.exe
*.out
*.elf
*.deb
*.rpm
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tar.xz
*.tgz
*.zip
*.xz
*.img
*.iso
!*.diffstat.txt

# --- python / editor / OS junk --------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# --- never commit nested repos or harness metadata ------------------------
# Nested .git directories make git treat the subtree as an unstaged gitlink,
# which silently publishes nothing while looking like it worked.
.git/
.gitmodules
.agents/
